  "sections": [
    {
      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "bwaquatics",
      "sourceUrl": "https://bwaquatics.com/products/parosphromenus-ornaticauda",
      "html": "<p>Parosphromenus ornaticauda (wild caught) is a small freshwater fish belonging to the family Osphronemidae. Adult males typically reach a maximum length of 3.5 cm (1.4 in), while females are slightly smaller.</p><ul><li>Temperament: peaceful, but males can be territorial</li><li>TDS: 0-60</li></ul>"
    },
    {
      "key": "habitat",
      "source": "bwaquatics",
      "sourceUrl": "https://bwaquatics.com/products/parosphromenus-ornaticauda",
      "html": "<p>In the wild, P. ornaticauda is found in slow-moving and shaded water bodies with a pH between 4.0 and 6.0 and a temperature range of 22 to 28 °C (71.6 to 82.4 °F).</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "aquariumSize",
      "source": "bwaquatics",
      "sourceUrl": "https://bwaquatics.com/products/parosphromenus-ornaticauda",
      "html": "<p>They are small fish, so it is recommended to keep them in groups of 5 in a tank of about 19 litres (5 gallons) or larger, unless breeding. In that case, they are best kept in pairs.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "diet",
      "source": "bwaquatics",
      "sourceUrl": "https://bwaquatics.com/products/parosphromenus-ornaticauda",
      "html": "<p>They feed on small aquatic invertebrates such as insect larvae and crustaceans. In the aquarium: blackworms, brine shrimp and water fleas. They only eat live food and must be trained to accept anything else. Adding dither fish tends to help them learn to take dry foods.</p>"
    }
  ],
